// stt_zhang2021_45nm
//
// GENERATED by from_paper.py from cells/sources.json.
// Edit sources.json, not this file; regenerate to change a value.
//
// Source: Zitong Zhang, Wenjie Wang, Pingping Yu, Yanfeng Jiang, "Cache performance of NV-STT-MRAM with scale effect and comparison with SRAM", International Journal of Electronics, 2021
// DOI:    10.1080/00207217.2021.1908630
// Tech:   STT-MRAM
// Node:   45 nm
//
// Geometry (verbatim from the paper):
//   1T1MTJ. Table 1 gives cell area 10 F^2 at aspect ratio 1.0 with a 6 F
//   access transistor. Note the same tension as DESTINY's shipped cell: a 6
//   F wide device does not fit inside 10 F^2, so treat the area as the MTJ
//   stack footprint rather than the full bit-cell. The paper's own Tables
//   3-4 sweep area over 10-30 F^2 and aspect ratio over 0.3-2.0, which is
//   the study this project mirrors for SOT.
//
// Provenance: 12 reported, 3 derived, 3 assumed.
// WARNING - these values are NOT from the paper:
//   MinSenseVoltage (mV) = 25  (DESTINY sample value)
//   ReadMode = voltage  (DESTINY default; the paper does not state a sensing scheme)
//   VoltageDropAccessDevice (V) = 0.15  (DESTINY sample value)
// CHECK: CellArea 10 F^2 cannot hold 1 access transistor(s) of width 6 F
// (needs about 18 F^2). Either the area is a cell-stack area excluding the
// transistor, or the two numbers come from different designs.
// CHECK: assumed (not measured) values: MinSenseVoltage (mV), ReadMode,
// VoltageDropAccessDevice (V)
// NOTE: The paper reports write latency to four decimal places across a 3x
// cell-area sweep while the value moves by under 2%. Treat their
// per-cell-area differences as noise, not signal; the reportable effect in
// their own data is the LEAKAGE change in Tables 5-6 (up to 42.1%), not
// the latency.
// NOTE: ReadCurrent solved by --auto-read; the paper's value did not admit
// a valid sense scheme at a safe MTJ read bias.

-MemCellType: MRAM                             // [reported] Table 1
-CellArea (F^2): 10                            // [reported] Table 1
-CellAspectRatio: 1                            // [reported] Table 1
-ResistanceOn (ohm): 7100                      // [reported] Table 1, Rp
-ResistanceOff (ohm): 15600                    // [reported] Table 1, Rap. TMR = 120%, consistent with the text's 'TMR set to 100%' only approximately.
-ReadMode: voltage                             // [assumed] DESTINY default; the paper does not state a sensing scheme
-ReadCurrent (uA): 28.169                      // [derived] solved: 0.20 V bias ceiling / R_on 7100 ohm = 28.17 uA, giving 239.4 mV sense margin again
-MinSenseVoltage (mV): 25                      // [assumed] DESTINY sample value
-ResetMode: current                            // [derived] current-driven MTJ
-ResetCurrent (uA): 29                         // [reported] Table 1, write current
-ResetPulse (ns): 10                           // [reported] Table 1, write pulse
-SetMode: current                              // [derived] current-driven MTJ
-SetCurrent (uA): 29                           // [reported] Table 1
-SetPulse (ns): 10                             // [reported] Table 1
-AccessType: CMOS                              // [reported] Table 1 gives an access CMOS width
-AccessCMOSWidth (F): 6                        // [reported] Table 1
-VoltageDropAccessDevice (V): 0.15             // [assumed] DESTINY sample value
-ProcessNode (nm): 45
